<title>SINGAPORE: Hotel Royal first half net sharply up.</title>
<headline>Hotel Royal first half net sharply up.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30 1996.</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore $ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		     2.56    vs    0.21</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)	  8.53    vs    0.71</p>
<p>    Turnover			 8.38    vs    8.53</p>
<p>    Other income		   1.75    vs    1.75</p>
<p>    Interest on borrowing	2.04    vs    1.76</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation  0.67    vs    1.43</p>
<p>    Tax				0.79    vs    0.66</p>
<p>Note - Hotel Royal Ltd said rental income from investments in Australia, New Zealand and Singapore has shown increases.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
